{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1014535-which-changing-breeds-can-be-corrupted","id":1014535,"title":"Which Changing Breeds can be corrupted?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-12-08T17:38:07-08:00","id":1014535,"title":"Which Changing Breeds can be corrupted?","content":"I know that by previous editions, the nuwisha's cant be corrupted (but now they can). So i was wondering, what can be corrupted and what cant be turned into a sort of blackspiral dancer / wyrm servant now a days?<br /> can a mokole become a servant of the wyrm ?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-08T18:20:47-08:00","id":1014561,"title":"","content":"Everything can be corrupted. That's kind of the point. Some Changers are just less likely to be.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-08T18:45:46-08:00","id":1014567,"title":"","content":"Wyrm Twisted Mokole lose themselves to Mnesis and become the memory-rewriting Mnetics.<br /> <br /> The Ananasi have possibly the 'best' fall overall, in that they become simply (and utterly) free of their Queen's control. Free to forge their own path, for good or ill.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.dropbox.com/s/ofii86boiyk38ng/DtDRandomForms.zip\" target=\"_blank\">Open the gates of Hell: Random Demon Generator.</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1X6qQzoAPrSRNzl3cQcMWasoPv3eK56sIlAOTeay61No/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Gather an army of Rage! Random Garou Generator.</a><br /> Shapeshifting Historian<br /> Writer - Werewolf: the Apocalypse, Werewolf: the Forsaken, Exalted 3e, TC: \u00c6on","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/167-nikink","name":"nikink","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"360"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-08T18:45:57-08:00","id":1014568,"title":"","content":"Not only <i>can</i> Mokole fall to the Wyrm, but a group of ones who have are central to the plot of Shattered Dreams.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5307-loomer","name":"loomer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5307_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-09T14:32:14-08:00","id":1014959,"title":"","content":"What some breeds cannot is to be changed by vampiric blood. All changers have some resistance to ghouling, and even more to the Embrace, and some go as far as to be completely immune (unless GM fiat). Right now I remember that Nuwisha, Corax and Mokole can't be ghouled nor Embraced. Corax and Mokole because Helios protects them that much, Nuwisha for reasons.<br /> <br /> The GM Fiat is relevant here because there are actual canon characters that are already exceptions. The greatest I know is Sobek, a 4th Generation Setite Mokole Abomination torpid somewhere in a temple in Egypt (obviously). It is explained, though, through ritual magic from Set himself.<br /> <br /> But that is it. It os hard as hell to turn most changers into vampire-related whatever, but <i>corrupted</i> they all can be, as easily as anyone else. And there is plenty of examples of corrupted individuals from all changers.<br /> <br /> Ananasi are a special case on most aspects, but the Kumo are there to show that they are as much prone to corruption by the Wyrm as anyone else. The difference is that an Ananasi can also be linked to the Wyrm without corruption, following the designs of their Totem-Queen.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-09T15:50:51-08:00","id":1014980,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1014535-which-changing-breeds-can-be-corrupted?p=1014959#post1014959\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What some breeds cannot is to be changed by vampiric blood. All changers have some resistance to ghouling, and even more to the Embrace, and some go as far as to be completely immune (unless GM fiat). Right now I remember that Nuwisha, Corax and Mokole can't be ghouled nor Embraced. Corax and Mokole because Helios protects them that much, Nuwisha for reasons.<br /> <br /> The GM Fiat is relevant here because there are actual canon characters that are already exceptions. The greatest I know is Sobek, a 4th Generation Setite Mokole Abomination torpid somewhere in a temple in Egypt (obviously). It is explained, though, through ritual magic from Set himself.<br /> <br /> But that is it. It os hard as hell to turn most changers into vampire-related whatever, but <i>corrupted</i> they all can be, as easily as anyone else. And there is plenty of examples of corrupted individuals from all changers.<br /> <br /> Ananasi are a special case on most aspects, but the Kumo are there to show that they are as much prone to corruption by the Wyrm as anyone else. The difference is that an Ananasi can also be linked to the Wyrm without corruption, following the designs of their Totem-Queen.</div> </div> </div> </div>Agreeing with most of this. Adding on the Ananasi that can't be embraced as far as I know. And while all changers <i>can</i> be corrupted, I wouldn't say that they can be as easily as everyone else. Every Changer is both aware of the corruption (something most people are oblivious to) and has tools to avoid or cleanse it. Unfortunately, it makes it that much worse when they do become corrupted. When changers fall, they tend to fall hard.<br /> <br /> And for Sobek, I think he is more rumored to be Mokole than actually proven to be. Having looked him up, he may not even actually exist. I'm not making a claim either way, but that is worth keeping in mind.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-10T12:44:03-08:00","id":1015341,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>idpersona</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1014535-which-changing-breeds-can-be-corrupted?p=1014980#post1014980\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Agreeing with most of this. Adding on the Ananasi that can't be embraced as far as I know. And while all changers <i>can</i> be corrupted, I wouldn't say that they can be as easily as everyone else. Every Changer is both aware of the corruption (something most people are oblivious to) and has tools to avoid or cleanse it. Unfortunately, it makes it that much worse when they do become corrupted. When changers fall, they tend to fall hard.<br /> <br /> And for Sobek, I think he is more rumored to be Mokole than actually proven to be. Having looked him up, he may not even actually exist. I'm not making a claim either way, but that is worth keeping in mind.</div> </div> </div> </div>On the Ananasi I'm not sure, but makes sense. I know they do infiltrate vampiric society, anyway, since they already can be emotionless, pallid and bloodsuckers.<br /> <br /> The &quot;as easily&quot; as everyone was meant to be in a natural basis. There is no rule about changers being more resistant by nature, but certainly they have by standard more resources than common people.<br /> <br /> Sobek is as true as any 4th generation. IIRC, he even have a character sheet, but I'm nor sure now. It doesn't matter, actually, if he is real in your chronicle, the point is that non-standard ways to overcome the natural resistance of changers to vampirism are a possibility for the ST, and already with examples in official books (even if the example is optional by itself).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-10T13:54:10-08:00","id":1015361,"title":"","content":"I do not even think that Kindred can drink Ananasi blood because of the arachnid proteins in their blood.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-10T15:39:51-08:00","id":1015385,"title":"","content":"Nothing says that a Kindred can't drink arthropod's blood, to begin with. It isn't out of question, or even of theme, that a vampire take sustenance from enough numbers of actual common spiders. So I see no reason for them not being able to drink an Ananasi's blood.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-10T15:56:15-08:00","id":1015394,"title":"","content":"It is from page 49 of the Ananasi book, under the Vampire section, it says that their blood is too alien for vampires to drink.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-10T17:47:29-08:00","id":1015426,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1014535-which-changing-breeds-can-be-corrupted?p=1015385#post1015385\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nothing says that a Kindred can't drink arthropod's blood, to begin with. It isn't out of question, or even of theme, that a vampire take sustenance from enough numbers of actual common spiders. So I see no reason for them not being able to drink an Ananasi's blood.</div> </div> </div> </div>Except that arthropods don't have blood. With an open circulatory system, what they have is hemolymph, a fluid with a much less homogenized set of chemicals than vertebrate blood. Also, most insects are way too tiny to have significant amounts of it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-10T22:19:14-08:00","id":1015548,"title":"","content":"Ok, so page 49 of Ananasi's book says it.<br /> <br /> I won't consider actual arthropods hemolymph, though, because it isn't relevant. Blood doesn't have the power to give motion to a corpse, either, much less to make this corpse reach another dimension to shape shadows or bend time to acquire velocity. A lot of vampire stories talk about lesser vampires who suck the life of vermin, including insects and arachnids. It isn't a necessary part of the vampire trope, but it is a valid one.<br /> <br /> Not against the game not going for it, though. At least not for the Ananasi, that are the weirdest of all changers, so it doesn't even have to have something to do with actual spiders. Specially if you consider that they are still changers, so partly human. Maybe they're edible for vampires, actual spiders. And the quantity problem can be overcome with, well, quantity.<br /> <br /> By the way, it doesn't have anything to do with Ananasi being immune to vampirism in any way. Either to be ghouled or Embraced the vampire doesn't have to drink a single drop of the victim's blood. It is the other way around, and Ananasi are <u>meant</u> to drink blood, even having their own Blood Pool. So they are quite receptive to vampire's blood, the opposite of other changers. I still think they are immune to vampirism, by the way, but for the metaphysical reasons of being already bloodsucking monsters.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-10T22:45:12-08:00","id":1015554,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1014535-which-changing-breeds-can-be-corrupted?p=1015548#post1015548\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> By the way, it doesn't have anything to do with Ananasi being immune to vampirism in any way. Either to be ghouled or Embraced the vampire doesn't have to drink a single drop of the victim's blood. It is the other way around, and Ananasi are <u>meant</u> to drink blood, even having their own Blood Pool. So they are quite receptive to vampire's blood, the opposite of other changers. I still think they are immune to vampirism, by the way, but for the metaphysical reasons of being already bloodsucking monsters.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know that I would come to the conclusion that Ananasi would be receptive to Vampire blood (the Bond or ghouling). I think all shapechangers, by virtue of their Gnosis/spirituality have an aversion/allergy. I wouldn't treat the Ananasi any differently than the system for Garou. Bonding them is doable, but not easy.<br /> <br /> And I come to that conclusion, for the same reason I believe they are immune to the embrace. Queen Ananasa does not share. Even the Kumo who supposedly escaped her aren't hunted down, because in theory they serve her purposes in doing so.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-10T23:06:01-08:00","id":1015566,"title":"","content":"When I said they were receptive to vampire's blood, I wasn't talking about Bonding or Ghouling. I was talking about drinking. Other changers react as if with a violent allergy to a vampire's blood. Ananasi drink blood, so I don't see them having any difficulty in swallowing vampire's blood.<br /> <br /> If I would talk about Bonding and Ghouling, I do not think that the Ananasi can be Ghouled, for the same reason I do not think they can be Embraced. But I do think they can be Bonded. You see, other changers can't be easily Bonded because they spit out or regurgitate Vitae most of the time, instead of actually consuming it. If Ananasi can drink vampire's blood, then they are prone to Bonding.<br /> <br /> That said, I wouldn't make their Bond into a normal one. They have weird shit with their emotions, with a few exceptions. Most Ananasi are cold as ice, a few are utterly emotionless, they are quite a psychopathic bunch. The Blood Bond of a species naturally hollowed of emotion could result in very weird things, from bland, weak bonds to a psychopath suddenly obsessed. Probably any result won't be very good for the vampire, anyway.<br /> <br /> About the system for ghouling and embracing a changer, I don't care about the others. The Ananasi are marked by weirdness, not being from Gaia nor anything the other changers are used to. Gnosis is your link to the Spirit, but the Spirit doesn't have to be inimical to vampires by default. I would make them immune because I can see them, as bloodsuckers already, being designed to drink cursed blood without contracting a curse that simply mimics them. As much as a vampire can't be ghouled or Embraced anew.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-10T23:15:57-08:00","id":1015570,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1014535-which-changing-breeds-can-be-corrupted?p=1015566#post1015566\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When I said they were receptive to vampire's blood, I wasn't talking about Bonding or Ghouling. I was talking about drinking. Other changers react as if with a violent allergy to a vampire's blood. Ananasi drink blood, so I don't see them having any difficulty in swallowing vampire's blood.<br /> <br /> If I would talk about Bonding and Ghouling, I do not think that the Ananasi can be Ghouled, for the same reason I do not think they can be Embraced. But I do think they can be Bonded. You see, other changers can't be easily Bonded because they spit out or regurgitate Vitae most of the time, instead of actually consuming it. If Ananasi can drink vampire's blood, then they are prone to Bonding.<br /> <br /> That said, I wouldn't make their Bond into a normal one. They have weird shit with their emotions, with a few exceptions. Most Ananasi are cold as ice, a few are utterly emotionless, they are quite a psychopathic bunch. The Blood Bond of a species naturally hollowed of emotion could result in very weird things, from bland, weak bonds to a psychopath suddenly obsessed. Probably any result won't be very good for the vampire, anyway.<br /> <br /> About the system for ghouling and embracing a changer, I don't care about the others. The Ananasi are marked by weirdness, not being from Gaia nor anything the other changers are used to. Gnosis is your link to the Spirit, but the Spirit doesn't have to be inimical to vampires by default. I would make them immune because I can see them, as bloodsuckers already, being designed to drink cursed blood without contracting a curse that simply mimics them. As much as a vampire can't be ghouled or Embraced anew.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is an interesting take on it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-11T01:53:57-08:00","id":1015603,"title":"","content":"On Sobek, there isn't a sheet for him. He has no write up. He is a myth told by Settite elders about how awesome Set is. These same people who say Caine is a myth, that Set was the first vampire that the Antedeluvians betrayed him, something that many would argue against. Now there may be a giant albino Crocodile shaped elder who's in charge of the cult. That doesn't prove he's an Mokole he could easily be an early Apostate Gangrel, or some other reason for having Protean or perhaps a unique Serpentis power, or just obfuscate or.. just a myth of the cult.<br /> <br /> <br /> That being said, Set laid down a full curse on Silent striders so he's got some serious dark blood magic power going on. That it might keep a Mokole from falling into eternal frenzy is possible, remember the failure point on Corax, Mokole and Rokea isn't they explode(that's kitsune) or it just fails(Nuwisha) its that they go into a Frenzy and never leave so it might be easier for Set to break that than other things with his magic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-11T11:56:21-08:00","id":1015755,"title":"","content":"Yes, Set would have been the founder and the grandmaster of Setite Sorcery, which means he would have access to 10th level Setite Sorcery Rituals. I would be more than willing to allow Embrace Mokole or Wither Ancestral Spirits as 10th level Setite Sorcery Rituals.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-11T12:56:11-08:00","id":1015791,"title":"","content":"A ritual to actually facilitate the Ghouling or Embrace of any changer could be as low as 5th level, depending on the chronicle's needs. Of course, at such &quot;low&quot; level it wouldn't include control over the creature. An before someone start to argue metaphysical reasons it shouldn't work, metaphysics is something you use to back-up your decisions, so the key is &quot;chronicle's needs&quot;. By default it should be exceedingly rare, anyway. I wouldn't question the power of Ur-Shulgi to make such a move, though, for Set it would be a piece of cake.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2715\" data-vbnamecard=\"2715\">Lian</a>, the evidence in favor of Sobek in this case in another thing. The way the canon deals with egyptian mythology. In short: the gods in general are explained as different supernatural beings, but with hugely consistent descriptions from vastly different narrators. They have a complex history also backed up by an astounding consistency between those narratives. And by that I mean consistency between the narratives of Children of Osiris, Followers of Set, Mage historians about the Cult of Isis, Silent Striders, several changers in Egypt, Mummies old and new, and so on. Egypt is the single most massive crossover of canon, with the clearest past, sometimes going even directly into reliable narratives, like some OoC pieces about Kemintiri's past as a Follower of Set that turned to the Daughters of Isis and them was Embraced by Set as punishment and torture.<br /> <br /> So indeed, Sobek is far from a certainty, and it is irrelevant to the matter at hand. But as a side note, the setting is already perfectly ready for it being true. Sobek would still remain as far from the weirdest piece of canon egyptian lore.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-11T13:56:19-08:00","id":1015824,"title":"","content":"So the closest thing I have seen to Ananasi being blood bound was from the Changing Breed short stories. I wasn't a fan of several of them but I did like the Ananasi story, in it it covered that Ananasi can't be blood bound due to a lack of emotion to begin with. She faked being ghouled in order to get information from vampires and play them to her advantage. I thought it was a creative spin on the Ananasi and vampires.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1179-celtspz","name":"CeltSPZ","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1179_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"835"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-12T20:54:57-08:00","id":1016389,"title":"","content":"I fully went to use Ananasi in some Vampire games of mine. A few of them went as further as to be regulars at Elysium.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-12T23:48:54-08:00","id":1016431,"title":"","content":"My ST says Ananasi are already Bonded, to their Queen, and from playing him he has a point...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2157-deejay","name":"deejay","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2157_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-13T05:06:57-08:00","id":1016499,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1014535-which-changing-breeds-can-be-corrupted?p=1015791#post1015791\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2715\" data-vbnamecard=\"2715\">Lian</a>, the evidence in favor of Sobek in this case in another thing. The way the canon deals with egyptian mythology. In short: the gods in general are explained as different supernatural beings, but with hugely consistent descriptions from vastly different narrators. They have a complex history also backed up by an astounding consistency between those narratives. And by that I mean consistency between the narratives of Children of Osiris, Followers of Set, Mage historians about the Cult of Isis, Silent Striders, several changers in Egypt, Mummies old and new, and so on. Egypt is the single most massive crossover of canon, with the clearest past, sometimes going even directly into reliable narratives, like some OoC pieces about Kemintiri's past as a Follower of Set that turned to the Daughters of Isis and them was Embraced by Set as punishment and torture.<br /> <br /> So indeed, Sobek is far from a certainty, and it is irrelevant to the matter at hand. But as a side note, the setting is already perfectly ready for it being true. Sobek would still remain as far from the weirdest piece of canon egyptian lore.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> It is important when one is complaining about Gm well really writer Fiat when there's no evidence whatsoever that Setites aren't a bunch of lying sacks of shit on the subject. There was a whole Craft dedicated to Sobek that had nothing to do with Vampires. Its not like he has a sheet, like Ur Shulgi, or Enkidu or Mithras<br /> <br /> And if you want him to exist there's all sorts of explanations for a Giant Crocodile Vampire that don't require ST fiat that the MOkole thing is wrong.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-13T07:01:51-08:00","id":1016525,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1014535-which-changing-breeds-can-be-corrupted?p=1016499#post1016499\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It is important when one is complaining about Gm well really writer Fiat when there's no evidence whatsoever that Setites aren't a bunch of lying sacks of shit on the subject. There was a whole Craft dedicated to Sobek that had nothing to do with Vampires. Its not like he has a sheet, like Ur Shulgi, or Enkidu or Mithras<br /> <br /> And if you want him to exist there's all sorts of explanations for a Giant Crocodile Vampire that don't require ST fiat that the MOkole thing is wrong.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ok, I'm thinking this is getting clearly off-topic, now, but I'm not sure if you didn't understand me, or if I didn't understand you here. Both bother me.<br /> <br /> I'm just saying that the setting supports the interpretation of Sobek actually being a Mokole Abomination. I'm not even saying that it is likely, or that I would use, just saying that it wouldn't be so strange to the setting. And it doesn't have nothing to do with fiat that the Mokole thing is wrong.<br /> <br /> That's all. WoD's Egypt already have this kind of thing, and a specific magic curse to bypass a natural impossibility is well withing the boundaries of the game. Similar curses and magical effects are all over the place, already. Ur-Shulgi, the sheet be damned, altered an entire clan's Weakness with quite literally the blink of an eye. Some Tribe Weaknesses, that are optional rules but a lot of people use them by default, are also curses. The Silent Striders, by the way, a curse from Set.<br /> <br /> But, again, just a possibility. You don't need any of this, but you can have it. A given ST can want Sobek as a Mokole, or to have a ritual that makes a Mokole vulnerable, because the chronicle will be improved this way and a giant intelligent crocodile of another kind won't do it, maybe the theme demands it to be an actual Mokole. So what? No one <u>have</u> to accept such, and if it isn't what the chronicle needs, I agree that there are simpler answers with plain weird crocodiles.<br /> <br /> What bothers you so much on it being possible, though?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-13T12:10:37-08:00","id":1016675,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1014535-which-changing-breeds-can-be-corrupted?p=1016525#post1016525\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What bothers you so much on it being possible, though?</div> </div> </div> </div>Personally, I agree with all of the points you make.<br /> <br /> That being said, what bothers me about the idea is that nothing short of Celestine Intervention is supposed be able to affect the possibility of becoming an Abomination. And while Set is powerful, I certainly place him below Celestine level.<br /> <br /> But again, story always trumps rules so for someone's story it could very well be possible. It just wouldn't be in a game I ran. Especially not a Werewolf game. If it were a Vampire game, then the Werewolf rules don't matter at all, so Sobek the Abomination would be a possibility, even if I see it as unnecessary.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-13T12:35:10-08:00","id":1016682,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>idpersona</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1014535-which-changing-breeds-can-be-corrupted?p=1016675#post1016675\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That being said, what bothers me about the idea is that nothing short of Celestine Intervention is supposed be able to affect the possibility of becoming an Abomination. And while Set is powerful, I certainly place him below Celestine level.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not necessarily, since 'Set mystically overpowers Helios' is not the only way a Mokole abomination might occur. What if Helios himself removed his blessing from this accursed creature, damning it to undeath?<br /> <br /> Interestingly, in Egyptian history circa 1500 BC, Sobek was a solar deity, equated with Ra. Perhaps a Mokole was the inspiration for such a theological shift, a mighty creature that considered itself a deity on par with mighty Helios. I can see Helios being irritated with the self-aggrandizing weredragon and rescinding his favor... which may have had the unintended consequence allowing the ill-fated Mokole to fall into the clutches of Set (or even seek out the legendary dark god, since the dragon's more traditional patron had deserted him).<br /> <br /> Not saying it has to be like this, but I don't think that Helios would lose to Set either... but Helios is kind of an arrogant prick, so I could see him casting one of his errant children into the darkness.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","name":"The Laughing Stranger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3695_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1010"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-13T12:55:38-08:00","id":1016691,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Laughing Stranger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1014535-which-changing-breeds-can-be-corrupted?p=1016682#post1016682\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not necessarily, since 'Set mystically overpowers Helios' is not the only way a Mokole abomination might occur. What if Helios himself removed his blessing from this accursed creature, damning it to undeath?<br /> <br /> Interestingly, in Egyptian history circa 1500 BC, Sobek was a solar deity, equated with Ra. Perhaps a Mokole was the inspiration for such a theological shift, a mighty creature that considered itself a deity on par with mighty Helios. I can see Helios being irritated with the self-aggrandizing weredragon and rescinding his favor... which may have had the unintended consequence allowing the ill-fated Mokole to fall into the clutches of Set (or even seek out the legendary dark god, since the dragon's more traditional patron had deserted him).<br /> <br /> Not saying it has to be like this, but I don't think that Helios would lose to Set either... but Helios is kind of an arrogant prick, so I could see him casting one of his errant children into the darkness.</div> </div> </div> </div>I like this explanation.<br /> I think that either Helios or other Mokole would have destroyed such a creature though. And to me, Helios &quot;rescinding his blessing&quot; is different from Helios actually interfering and helping Set embrace a Mokole, which according to the Abomination wording is what would be required. Even fallen/corrupt Fera get that Gnosis roll to die in peace.<br /> <br /> But thank you. This is at least a more plausible explanation than the nothing the books give us to go on.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-13T14:15:37-08:00","id":1016728,"title":"","content":"Set could simply act with opportunity. Helios rescind the blessing, Set gets to do the Embrace. As an Ante, it isn't too hard to think that Set could have a number of ways to know of the hapless creature and go for the &quot;prize&quot;. Also it wouldn't be hard for Sobek to seek Set out of spite, because Set was pretty famous at the time.<br /> <br /> About Set being or not as strong as Helios to bypass the protection, it is a matter of interpretation and taste.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-13T14:18:30-08:00","id":1016731,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1014535-which-changing-breeds-can-be-corrupted?p=1016728#post1016728\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Set could simply act with opportunity. Helios rescind the blessing, Set gets to do the Embrace. As an Ante, it isn't too hard to think that Set could have a number of ways to know of the hapless creature and go for the &quot;prize&quot;. Also it wouldn't be hard for Sobek to seek Set out of spite, because Set was pretty famous at the time.</div> </div> </div> </div>Set still wouldn't have the power to influence the roll to die for the Mokole. Set could seize on the opportunity to give it a try, but the Mokole would still just die 99% of the time.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1014535-which-changing-breeds-can-be-corrupted?p=1016728#post1016728\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> About Set being or not as strong as Helios to bypass the protection, it is a matter of interpretation and taste.</div> </div> </div> </div>And I put Ante's firmly below the Sun in power level.<br /> Again, for a Vampire game, none of this matters even a little bit. But for a Werewolf or Crossover game, I wouldn't let it happen.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-13T14:48:42-08:00","id":1016752,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>idpersona</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1014535-which-changing-breeds-can-be-corrupted?p=1016731#post1016731\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Set still wouldn't have the power to influence the roll to die for the Mokole. Set could seize on the opportunity to give it a try, but the Mokole would still just die 99% of the time.<br /> <br /> <br /> And I put Ante's firmly below the Sun in power level.<br /> Again, for a Vampire game, none of this matters even a little bit. But for a Werewolf or Crossover game, I wouldn't let it happen.</div> </div> </div> </div>Definitely. From the point of view of games that aren't Vampire, a lot of the vaunted power of the Antediluvians and earlier vampires can be put down to the protagonists of a typical V:tM game being less potent dilutions of their progenitors, and therefore having no written-in defenses of any kind. They're &quot;begat&quot; of that blood, and therefore beholden to it and unable to struggle significantly to avoid its pull.<br /> <br /> Other games, however, focus on monsters with no relation to any kind of vampire, or the themes of V:tM, and so the lower generations of vampires can be reasonably set up as more hype than god. Assuming, of course, you even use Kindred in the first place.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-15T22:39:43-08:00","id":1017970,"title":"","content":"It's also perfectly possible that the ancient Egyptians had it right and Set <i>is</i> a god, just one primarily served by a cult of vampires that named themselves after him.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-16T04:27:39-08:00","id":1018021,"title":"","content":"Its easy to dismiss possibilities in favor of preferred interpretations, and to ignore the possibilities brought by crossing elements, even without a crossover game proper.<br /> <br /> Set being so strong is too stingy for Werewolf because Set is a Vampire? Werewolf have already things like &quot;Fomori&quot; with as much power as an Incarna. The Hydra have quite a bunch under her control, and under Werewolf cosmology everything is ultimately linked to the Umbra. Why not apply that? The Antediluvian can be Banes or Fomori of such power as to become equivalent to the Tribes's Totems. Maybe Set's rites are ways to commune with the Wyrm itself, in order to protect its most daring feats from interference from the Celestines.<br /> <br /> Heck, it could very well be true in a Vampire game, why not in Werewolf? To downplay the other games power-players is certainly fair, but a bit of lacking in creativity at some times. If you want to incorporate them (if not, it is all irrelevant, anyway), it is better to adapt them to the actual cosmology you're using.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-16T09:14:27-08:00","id":1018117,"title":"","content":"I don't want to get into a whole mechanical argument when this is really about fluff and story telling, but Mokole don't roll dice like Garou do to die when undergoing an Embrace. They just die at sunrise after going on a rampage, because Helios wills it.<br /> <br /> If that auto-death ability was removed because of some plot-related happenstance, Mokole don't have some backup 'almost certainly die' suicide power like the Garou do. The rules for Garou resisting the Embrace specifically note they are Gaia's favored children and that is why they are granted this out. There is no reason to expect that Mokole also would have this ability granted them.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","name":"The Laughing Stranger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3695_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1010"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-16T09:29:21-08:00","id":1018124,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1014535-which-changing-breeds-can-be-corrupted?p=1016525#post1016525\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> What bothers you so much on it being possible, though?</div> </div> </div> </div>I am not bothered by it being possible. Games are meant to be played. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1014535-which-changing-breeds-can-be-corrupted?p=1016525#post1016525\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;The GM Fiat is relevant here because there are actual canon characters that are already exceptions. The greatest I know is Sobek, a 4th Generation Setite Mokole Abomination torpid somewhere in a temple in Egypt (obviously). It is explained, though, through ritual magic from Set himself.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Sobek is not a Canon character. He is a MYTH. He could potentially exist, or he could not. There's all sorts of options for him. But spreading that there is any such character given a writeup as anything more than &quot;Bullshit settites tell&quot; is the issue. That book is filled with all sorts of bullshit the Settites all of the clan books are filled with bullshit the clans tell themselves. Lies and self serving half truths.<br /> <br /> If you want to say that myth is true, go right ahead. There's more than enough ways for it to happen but stop portraying it like its a certainty or that people who take a different interpretation are some how wrong.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-16T11:09:12-08:00","id":1018148,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Laughing Stranger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1014535-which-changing-breeds-can-be-corrupted?p=1018117#post1018117\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't want to get into a whole mechanical argument when this is really about fluff and story telling, but Mokole don't roll dice like Garou do to die when undergoing an Embrace. They just die at sunrise after going on a rampage, because Helios wills it.<br /> <br /> If that auto-death ability was removed because of some plot-related happenstance, Mokole don't have some backup 'almost certainly die' suicide power like the Garou do. The rules for Garou resisting the Embrace specifically note they are Gaia's favored children and that is why they are granted this out. There is no reason to expect that Mokole also would have this ability granted them.</div> </div> </div> </div>I actually hadn't thought of it that way. From the descriptions I had assumed that the Gnosis roll to die peacefully was a Gaia infused thing for all Fera (possibly not the Ananasi), and that the Fera special rules (Mokole, Corax, Nuwisha, maybe Kitsune) override and replace it. Looking back, I see that it was an inference that isn't actually spelled out, but I think going forward I will still go with that assumption for my own games. The rules on Fera-Vampires are usually limited to a single line or 2 in any given book so I don't think it's that big of a leap to lean on the several paragraphs on the subject spelled out for the Garou. I do not agree though that the rules for Garou are because they are &quot;Gaia's favored children&quot; since several other Fera also follow those same rules (Ratkin, Bastet, Gurahl off the top of my head).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-16T12:07:41-08:00","id":1018165,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2715\" data-vbnamecard=\"2715\">Lian</a>, I'm on the impression that you ignored everything I posted after that. I'll wait until you tell if I'm wrong or not before giving proper answer, since it will affect my answer.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3695_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3695\" data-vbnamecard=\"3695\">The Laughing Stranger</a>, though you're right on a strict interpretation, I don't think the reverse less probable, given Garous' inclination to pride and self-aggrandizement. Both are equally valid, since the absence of further development can be explained on the rarity of it even being a question. That said, I don't think it would be hard to remove this second layer of resistance once the first was done with.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-16T12:44:02-08:00","id":1018185,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1014535-which-changing-breeds-can-be-corrupted?p=1018165#post1018165\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2715\" data-vbnamecard=\"2715\">Lian</a>, I'm on the impression that you ignored everything I posted after that. I'll wait until you tell if I'm wrong or not before giving proper answer, since it will affect my answer.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3695_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3695\" data-vbnamecard=\"3695\">The Laughing Stranger</a>, though you're right on a strict interpretation, I don't think the reverse less probable, given Garous' inclination to pride and self-aggrandizement. Both are equally valid, since the absence of further development can be explained on the rarity of it even being a question. That said, I don't think it would be hard to remove this second layer of resistance once the first was done with.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>'<br /> The Mokole's deal comes from a Celestine. The overall deal of dying comes from something bigger. I don't think that it'd be easier to remove that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-16T12:49:46-08:00","id":1018188,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1014535-which-changing-breeds-can-be-corrupted?p=1018185#post1018185\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">'<br /> The Mokole's deal comes from a Celestine. The overall deal of dying comes from something bigger. I don't think that it'd be easier to remove that.</div> </div> </div> </div>That rule about rolling Gnosis to die is only listed as an ability for Garou, not everything with Gnosis. Otherwise it would have been discussed alongside the other outcomes of attempting to embrace the other Fera, but instead it talks about how the Mokole go on rampages, for example. Indeed, if they were able to roll Gnosis to kill themselves, it would conflict with the berserker outcome that is supposed to happen when Mokole are embraced.<br /> <br /> I think the Changing Breeds are supposed to have defenses against being turned, but I think those defenses vary by breed and have specific outcomes. Nuwisha, Mokole, Corax, Kitsune, ect, all have abilities that prevent them from being turned (usually!). Garou, Bastet and Gurahl have defenses too, but they are not quite as foolproof. I don't see why the other breeds would <i>also </i>have the defense specifically offered to the Garou.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3695,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","user":"The Laughing Stranger","date":". 12-16-2016, 03:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","name":"The Laughing Stranger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3695_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1010"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-16T13:17:11-08:00","id":1018202,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Laughing Stranger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1014535-which-changing-breeds-can-be-corrupted?p=1018188#post1018188\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That rule about rolling Gnosis to die is only listed as an ability for Garou, not everything with Gnosis. Otherwise it would have been discussed alongside the other outcomes of attempting to embrace the other Fera, but instead it talks about how the Mokole go on rampages, for example. Indeed, if they were able to roll Gnosis to kill themselves, it would conflict with the berserker outcome that is supposed to happen when Mokole are embraced.<br /> <br /> I think the Changing Breeds are supposed to have defenses against being turned, but I think those defenses vary by breed and have specific outcomes. Nuwisha, Mokole, Corax, Kitsune, ect, all have abilities that prevent them from being turned (usually!). Garou, Bastet and Gurahl have defenses too, but they are not quite as foolproof. I don't see why the other breeds would <i>also </i>have the defense specifically offered to the Garou.</div> </div> </div> </div>Because it's not specific to the Garou, as noted above. In the absence of auto-die, it is therefore not at all unreasonable to assume that they still most likely die. Quite frankly, not putting the option to simply die in seems like one of the many, many oversights of Werewolf, like what happens to the mechanics of Renown-based Gifts when their mechanics are copied over to other character types but they don't have the same type of Renown in said character type. Are you going to make Dragon's Tongue do no damage to enemies because Mokole don't have Cunning Renown and the mechanics say &quot;as the Pumonca Gift: Thunderbolt&quot;?. Do members of the Beast Courts find that their use of Fu Xi's Honor or Rage of the Nest Mother fail to function because they have Virtue Renown instead of Honor Renown? Because a yes to those questions would seem very, very silly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-16T13:29:31-08:00","id":1018207,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1014535-which-changing-breeds-can-be-corrupted?p=1018202#post1018202\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Because it's not specific to the Garou, as noted above. In the absence of auto-die, it is therefore not at all unreasonable to assume that they still most likely die. Quite frankly, not putting the option to simply die in seems like one of the many, many oversights of Werewolf, like what happens to the mechanics of Renown-based Gifts when their mechanics are copied over to other character types but they don't have the same type of Renown in said character type.</div> </div> </div> </div>You didn't note anything, you just said 'I assume this is how it works.' I say it isn't an oversight. Your other cut-and dried examples of oversights don't have any direct bearing or consequence on this situation. Whether a Mokole that managed to survive the dawn could have actually killed itself earlier with a Gnosis roll seems pretty bizarre and debatable. It doesn't even make sense in a sequence of events that they get both because the Garou way of preventing the embrace happens before they turn into an abomination, whereas the Mokole method of abomination prevention kills them after (up to) a night of slaughter. If the Mokole had the Garou's method of abomination prevention, that Gnosis roll to die should be kicking in before a Mokole rampages in the first place, since the creature can still exist as an abomination for up to a full night.<br /> <br /> But again, the whole situation is very much off the reservation in the first place- if Mokole abominations don't fit into how you view WtA, whether they are allowed to attempt suicide via Gnosis is probably going to be a non-issue.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3695,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","user":"The Laughing Stranger","date":". 12-16-2016, 04:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","name":"The Laughing Stranger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3695_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1010"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-16T14:15:32-08:00","id":1018220,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Laughing Stranger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1014535-which-changing-breeds-can-be-corrupted?p=1018207#post1018207\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You didn't note anything,</div> </div> </div> </div>Other people did. Specifically, the &quot;special Garou&quot; relationship is shared by a number of other breeds. The Ajaba and Gurahl basically have carbon copies of it, so it's obviously not a unique Garou feature.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> you just said 'I assume this is how it works.' I say it isn't an oversight. Your other cut-and dried examples of oversights don't have any direct bearing or consequence on this situation. </div> </div> </div>Except in that most of the moving parts of the system never receive deep attention. And this is one of them.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Whether a Mokole that managed to survive the dawn could have actually killed itself earlier with a Gnosis roll seems pretty bizarre and debatable. It doesn't even make sense in a sequence of events that they get both because the Garou way of preventing the embrace happens before they turn into an abomination, whereas the Mokole method of abomination prevention kills them after (up to) a night of slaughter. If the Mokole had the Garou's method of abomination prevention, that Gnosis roll to die should be kicking in before a Mokole rampages in the first place, since the creature can still exist as an abomination for up to a full night. </div> </div> </div>Well, the Mokole and Rokea are basically about as alive as a victim of Hokuto Shinken's accupoint strikes after the vitae hits, so it's not really a big conundrum. Just a corpse thrashing around.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But again, the whole situation is very much off the reservation in the first place- if Mokole abominations don't fit into how you view WtA, whether they are allowed to attempt suicide via Gnosis is probably going to be a non-issue. </div> </div> </div>That filters back into the &quot;antediluvians only plot device to thinner-blooded, weaksauce vampires&quot; argument I put forward.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-16T14:54:08-08:00","id":1018232,"title":"","content":"I think it is also worth nothing that the entire discussion at this point relies on a plot point that is entirely ST fiat. Whether or not a Fera (in this case, Mokole) has a supposed second layer of defense already hinges on the idea that Helios can and will withdraw the rampage-until-dawn-and-die layer. We don't have any idea if this is even possible since there are zero examples in game of it happening. But if you, as a ST, decide that Helios can withdraw said benefit (if it can be called that), then he is also able to interfere with the Gnosis roll (being a Celestine). I just don't see why he would do either of those things.<br /> <br /> As an extension of this thought though, if the Mokole loses this blessing (and Helios's favor in general), would said Mokole still have the vulnerability to gold?<br /> <br /> Also...and this may only be funny to me. This entire tangent can be traced back to a character that in setting, is a rumor. Even from and OOC point of view, Sobek is a rumor. There is no factual evidence that such a creature actually exists. And it would be far easier in setting to account for Sobek as having a unique Elder level Serpentis power than it is to jump through (several at this point) ST fiat hoops to make this character even possible.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-16T15:09:44-08:00","id":1018233,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1014535-which-changing-breeds-can-be-corrupted?p=1018220#post1018220\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Other people did. Specifically, the &quot;special Garou&quot; relationship is shared by a number of other breeds. The Ajaba and Gurahl basically have carbon copies of it, so it's obviously not a unique Garou feature.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Ajaba and Gurahl do have very similar abilities, which says nothing about the other breeds who are <i>not</i> noted as specifically having Gnosis-suicide as an option.<br /> <br /> But as idpersona said, this all seems more likely to be something akin to a vampire using Serpentis 7: Divine Image and appearing as Sobek, rather than a special snowflake Mokole abomination.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","name":"The Laughing Stranger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3695_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1010"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-16T21:15:02-08:00","id":1018327,"title":"","content":"Even as a rumor, I wouldn't call it zero examples. It is, at the very least, an idea. My main point, by the way, isn't about Sobek being real (it is just a rumor), but being an idea that can be real or not. And the <u>idea</u> is canon, even if its veracity isn't stated, specially because its falseness isn't, either. But I digress.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3695_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3695\" data-vbnamecard=\"3695\">The Laughing Stranger</a>, the point on the Gnosis roll is that it definitely IS an oversight. And a very acceptable oversight. This discussion is about a very remote possibility of a specific ritual to get rid of a stated rule. Even considering it possible, still remains as very, very far from the default working of the game, and an actual means to make it happen wasn't ever presented. It would be really strange for them to go so far as to address an eventual loss of Helio's protection. If it had been done, then the possibility would be a given and this discussion pointless, because them a way to do so would be a given. So, yes, this roll is absent on the rules, but it means nothing, really.<br /> <br /> About reasoning it, there are several ways. As SOS pointed, you could simply say that Helios drives the corpse of the &quot;Abomination&quot; to be a rampaging Beast for some hour before destroying it with pyrotechnics. It doesn't need for the Mokol\u00e9 to be alive, so the whole should make the Gnosis roll moot, and that isn't the same as non-existent.<br /> <br /> But, again, if someone can get rid of Helios' blessing, the Gnosis roll shouldn't be so much of a problem. Even Gaia being a greater spirit, it is also a fairly non-interfering one. If it was so hard to deal with, then Gaia wouldn't need warriors to begin with.<br /> <br /> Just to finish, a thought I had for some time in this discussion. I find it poor to write down the possibility of said event based on Helios' standing, or Gaia's. Forget about Set, said ritual could be performed by any BSD or whatever, drawing power of any Wyrm or Weaver-aligned entity, with the help of any McGuffin. The <u>possibility</u> of a unique event deconstructing any set piece of the setting is a staple of fiction and a source of options to the ST. It isn't the same as saying that it happened or whatever, and the very impossibility by default means gives it significance. But to simply state that impossible is actually completely impossible by any means serves only to cut on sources of theme and drama.<br /> <br /> If Helios and Gaia are too powerful for you to have a chance at circumvent them even in a single case, so the changers can go home. The war is pointless, the gods can take care of themselves. The game is, though, ultimately based on the premises that the gods need their subjects to deal with shit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-16T21:35:29-08:00","id":1018331,"title":"","content":"If nothing else, 'evil' should be able to cloud the perceptions of the major spiritual entities. I think that would be the major point of any ritual to make a Mokole Abomination, it would have to be sufficient to cloud the perception of Helios (level nine or ten).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-16T23:07:23-08:00","id":1018356,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1014535-which-changing-breeds-can-be-corrupted?p=1018331#post1018331\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If nothing else, 'evil' should be able to cloud the perceptions of the major spiritual entities. I think that would be the major point of any ritual to make a Mokole Abomination, it would have to be sufficient to cloud the perception of Helios (level nine or ten).</div> </div> </div> </div>I think trying to assign such an event to a level is actually less helpful than discussing this as purely a thought exercise. Because having a level (in this case, 9 or 10 stated) means you then have to compare it to the power it's trying to overcome (in this case, a Celestine). I actually prefer <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar5826_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"5826\" data-vbnamecard=\"5826\">monteparnas</a> 's approach. Including some McGuffin and specific unrepeatable circumstances, as opposed to saying Set just can.<br /> <br /> And who knows. Taking a leap and saying Sobek is a real thing and is/was Mokole. Perhaps the Vampiric fate of Mokole was only partially overcome. Maybe just the bit about detonating at sunrise is what's been prevented, and a Mokole Abomination has been laying staked somewhere in a forgotten temple for the last few thousand years. So whatever power and work and magical McGuffin(s) went into it, and all that really happened is you have this wretched, likely mindless helpless creature lost somewhere wishing for death eternally. That is obviously only one possibility of many, but I think it is far more interesting than hand waiving this rumor and real because &quot;Set did it and he's awesome&quot;.<br /> <br /> And again, I would be more willing to run this idea in a Vampire game, where Werewolf cosmology/rules don't matter. Things are a lot more cut and dry with rules from the WtA end. Though obviously from these last couple of pages, it isn't perfectly clear.<br /> <br /> <br /> And asking again because I'm curious. Anyone have thoughts on whether or not Sobek should be vulnerable to gold if Helios has turned his back on said Mokole so completely?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-17T00:43:34-08:00","id":1018370,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1014535-which-changing-breeds-can-be-corrupted?p=1018327#post1018327\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Even as a rumor, I wouldn't call it zero examples. It is, at the very least, an idea. My main point, by the way, isn't about Sobek being real (it is just a rumor), but being an idea that can be real or not. And the <u>idea</u> is canon, even if its veracity isn't stated, specially because its falseness isn't, either. But I digress.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> It is zero examples. There's all sorts of canon held beliefs by groups that are 100 percent false. The book which it comes from is filed with statements that people casually treat as false(like Set being the first vampire)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-17T08:33:55-08:00","id":1018464,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar805_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"805\" data-vbnamecard=\"805\">idpersona</a>, I think that the gold would stand as a weakness. It doesn't represents a &quot;blessing&quot; of sorts, but the symbolic touch of Helios itself, as silver represents the touch of Luna. It is more in the sense of your resilience not standing against your lord. It would be a reasonable approach to get rid of the vulnerability, but I think it would remain.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2715\" data-vbnamecard=\"2715\">Lian</a>, there is not. Though surely there are things almost all readers casually treat as false, there is very little in the canon that can be said 100% false for sure. But since I remain in the impression that you didn't read most of my previous posts, and you didn't answered my question about it, I have no condition to answer you further. I cannot currently write so much more than I already do, until the tendinitis heals.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-17T09:33:26-08:00","id":1018485,"title":"","content":"[QUOTE=monteparnas;n1018464]<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar805_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"805\" data-vbnamecard=\"805\">idpersona</a>, I think that the gold would stand as a weakness. It doesn't represents a &quot;blessing&quot; of sorts, but the symbolic touch of Helios itself, as silver represents the touch of Luna. It is more in the sense of your resilience not standing against your lord. It would be a reasonable approach to get rid of the vulnerability, but I think it would remain.<br /> <br /> Werewolf abominations are still vulnerable to silver, so I don't see why things would change for a Mokole...<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1179-celtspz","name":"CeltSPZ","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1179_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"835"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-17T09:44:22-08:00","id":1018490,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CeltSPZ</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1014535-which-changing-breeds-can-be-corrupted?p=1018485#post1018485\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Werewolf abominations are still vulnerable to silver, so I don't see why things would change for a Mokole...</div> </div> </div> </div>Not arguing either way (since I actually want opinions). But the reason I was asking is because in the proposed example, Helios is actually turning his back on the Mokole. &quot;Normal&quot; Garou Abominations still having the silver vulnerability haven't had Luna turn away from them. And the Mokole Abomination would still have a silver vulnerability since in this scenario Luna theoretically hasn't forsaken Sobek.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-17T09:49:20-08:00","id":1018493,"title":"","content":"The Garou weakness to silver is caused by Luna's curse on the Garou. I don't know what the Mokole as a whole might have done to make Helios mad at them, but assuming the cause of their vulnerability to gold is also a curse, I don't know why that earlier curse would be rescinded if a particular Mokole were to be cursed and allowed to transform into a vampire.<br /> <br /> <br /> Man, I just used the word 'curse' a few times too many... but you get the idea.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","name":"The Laughing Stranger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3695_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1010"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-17T09:59:33-08:00","id":1018497,"title":"","content":"I always viewed the Silver weakness as being less of a curse and more of a tradeoff for Rage/power sort of thing. Otherwise, Luna (and Helios) went around cursing a ton of Gaia's creations.<br /> <br /> The Corax myth about Helios would at least explain a curse from him on them. But most of the other Shifters don't have something along those lines. And Coyote/Nuwisha who are arguably deserving of a Curse from Luna get off with her turning her back on them (in their telling) and so are free of it.<br /> <br /> All of this sort of thing is fairly inconsistent throughout the books.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-17T10:05:00-08:00","id":1018499,"title":"","content":"Probably they are fairly twisted interpretations. Most changers didn't had that a significant talk with either spirit for quite a long time. In the end, most of what changers believe is more religion and myth than fact, even if the core beliefs are demonstrable truth.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-17T10:26:11-08:00","id":1018504,"title":"","content":"I think that while Helios maybe turning his back so to speak on the Mok-pire (so much faster to type then Mokole vampire, or mokole abomination, granted the time saved with my just minted term was wasted on typing this aside) I think the weakness could still remain out of spite, something to remind the critter what it was, and allow for the more faithful Mokole to have a weapon to put it down (Sun Enfleshed, not only do you glow like the sun, but all natural attacks count as gold).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1179-celtspz","name":"CeltSPZ","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1179_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"835"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-17T11:22:51-08:00","id":1018520,"title":"","content":"I could have sworn that the weakness to silver is supposedly because of misuse of the gift of rage during the First War of Tears, but that might just be me mis-remembering something.<br /> <br /> Really cool idea, Celt... not sure the name is gonna catch on, though :P!<br /> <br /> Honestly, I like the idea of a Sobek being a unique monster the players can almost literally unearth and then destroy. Going on a quest for Helios and killing a blasphemous legendary evil with copious amounts of fire sounds pretty rad. Even if the thing turns out to 'just' be an incredibly old Settite, it'll still burn like all the rest...<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","name":"The Laughing Stranger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3695_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1010"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-17T11:52:53-08:00","id":1018532,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Laughing Stranger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1014535-which-changing-breeds-can-be-corrupted?p=1018520#post1018520\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I could have sworn that the weakness to silver is supposedly because of misuse of the gift of rage during the First War of Tears, but that might just be me mis-remembering something.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Did Shattered Dreams add on another War of Tears somewhere? Did someone kill the Bunyip twice?<br /> <br /> Overall, incidentally, the game doesn't take the major tack that the condition of any given Garou is a curse, but a responsibility. Silver and gold are part of the chiminage to attain it, not unlike how kami &quot;taints&quot; take the form of proscriptions and such to balance out any powers that they get.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-17T12:52:38-08:00","id":1018554,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1014535-which-changing-breeds-can-be-corrupted?p=1018532#post1018532\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Did Shattered Dreams add on another War of Tears somewhere? Did someone kill the Bunyip twice?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, pretty sure that was the one where they killed all the anally retentive dinosaurs, but I am not 100% sure.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3695,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","user":"The Laughing Stranger","date":". 12-17-2016, 03:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","name":"The Laughing Stranger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3695_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1010"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-17T13:05:41-08:00","id":1018557,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Laughing Stranger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1014535-which-changing-breeds-can-be-corrupted?p=1018554#post1018554\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah, pretty sure that was the one where they killed all the anally retentive dinosaurs, but I am not 100% sure.</div> </div> </div> </div>And a fine job ye did, too!<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-24T18:42:02-08:00","id":1021762,"title":"","content":"I thought Mokole could be embraced into abominations, but they had a single night of full out frenzy, then instinctively greet the sun?<br /> <br /> Or did that change between editions?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-25T00:39:11-08:00","id":1021889,"title":"","content":"Nope, that's still it.<br /> <br /> We just called it &quot;can't be embraced&quot; in this thread for ease of reference.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"